description:
DEPRECATED, use tool-set-visibility. Show (Enabled=true) or hide (Enabled=false) MCP tools by name; a hidden tool is left out of tools/list but still runs when called by name.

Argument types — give these arguments as RQL values (as in rql-mutate): {key: value, …}, [a, b], "text", 1.5, true, ref("GameObject#12") from a query result, unity.find("Name"); leave out keys you do not need:
ToolToggleInput {Name string (Name of the MCP tool to show or hide.), Enabled bool (Whether the tool is listed to MCP clients (true) or hidden from tools/list (false). A hidden tool still runs when called by name.)}

